{"data": [{"author_id": "2084142065307533313", "created_at": "2026-10-22T02:14:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113091557566156809"], "id": "2113091557566156809", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 24, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A 10,000-GPU cluster draws 20-40 MW. That's a small town's grid load. Microsoft, Meta, and Google have announced multi-gigawatt datacenter plans, but utility upgrades require 3-5 years of permitting and construction. You can lease GPUs in weeks. You cannot lease a substation.", "url": "https://x.com/BoboLinNotes/status/2113091557566156809"}, {"author_id": "1165159200470650881", "created_at": "2026-10-22T20:27:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113366724066382043"], "id": "2113366724066382043", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 53, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Meta has described the first phase of Prometheus, its gigawatt-scale AI training cluster in New Albany, Ohio.\n\nThe first phase is finished, and Meta used it to train the Muse models. Meta says it is working toward about 1 million GPUs. Today the cluster runs two NVIDIA platforms.", "url": "https://x.com/AIQuanting/status/2113366724066382043"}, {"author_id": "1936627678582636544", "created_at": "2026-10-22T12:17:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113243351965450354"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 14, "start": 9, "tag": "IREN"}]}, "id": "2113243351965450354", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 46, "impression_count": 7282, "like_count": 105, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "DSX POD: $IREN’s Path to Rapid Compute Deployment Is Now Crystal Clear\n\nI still have saved on my computer the discussion between IREN COO Kent and a Lenovo vice president in March this year, as well as the discussion with NVIDIA representatives in September. Both covered the", "url": "https://x.com/franklee6924T/status/2113243351965450354"}, {"author_id": "1523772134799015936", "created_at": "2026-10-22T13:24:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113260260345688248"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 5, "start": 0, "tag": "NBIS"}]}, "id": "2113260260345688248", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 136, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$NBIS had a packed GTC Berlin. Here are the highlights from the conference and surrounding announcements that stood out to me as a Nebius investor:\n\n1. 1 GW of Vera Rubin coming in 2027\n\nMarc said Nebius has a gigawatt of Vera Rubin capacity coming next year, with significant", "url": "https://x.com/family_remy/status/2113260260345688248"}, {"author_id": "1935410940020928512", "created_at": "2026-10-22T05:15:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113137116637216935"], "id": "2113137116637216935", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 44, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "xAI has brought Colossus 2 online, making it the first gigawatt-scale AI datacenter in the world. The Memphis complex runs on on-site gas turbines through subsidiary Solaris Energy, with expansion now crossing the Mississippi state line to add hundreds of thousands of GPUs. The", "url": "https://x.com/VeduisWeb/status/2113137116637216935"}, {"author_id": "1935410940020928512", "created_at": "2026-10-22T04:14:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113121767359398237"], "id": "2113121767359398237", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "xAI has brought Colossus 2 online, making it the first gigawatt-scale AI datacenter in the world. The Memphis complex runs on on-site gas turbines through subsidiary Solaris Energy, with expansion now crossing the Mississippi state line to add hundreds of thousands of GPUs. The", "url": "https://x.com/VeduisWeb/status/2113121767359398237"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113654638310203392"]}, "author_id": "2103141510799642624", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:31:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113654639857955257"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Every human predicts the future of AI. We keep the receipts.", "display_url": "aipredictionindex.com/predictions/?p…", "end": 203, "expanded_url": "https://www.aipredictionindex.com/predictions/?person=Elon%20Musk", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111887984542756864/9dGOX96O?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2111887984542756864/9dGOX96O?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 180, "status": 200, "title": "AI Prediction Index", "unwound_url": "https://www.aipredictionindex.com/predictions/?person=Elon%20Musk", "url": "https://t.co/h06LF9OK7Y"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/PBp5eE9p2Y", "end": 227, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/aipredictionx/status/2113654639857955257/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113654638310203392", "start": 204, "url": "https://t.co/PBp5eE9p2Y"}]}, "id": "2113654639857955257", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🟡 \"First Gigawatt training cluster in the world.\"\nElon Musk, 2026\n\nEpoch's satellite read: ~350 MW in January, ~946 MW by September. The 1.5GW April upgrade now projected Q1 2027.\nhttps://t.co/h06LF9OK7Y https://t.co/PBp5eE9p2Y", "url": "https://x.com/aipredictionx/status/2113654639857955257"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113427084563320832"]}, "author_id": "494126672", "created_at": "2026-10-23T00:27:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113427089713955012"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/TMrkWPVHFK", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TSC/status/2113427089713955012/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113427084563320832", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/TMrkWPVHFK"}, {"display_url": "x.com/i/status/21133…", "end": 319, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/i/status/2113313944966177176", "start": 296, "url": "https://t.co/rPa0aLOklE"}]}, "id": "2113427089713955012", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 42, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113313944966177176", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "nvidia built a thing that watches every gpu, cable and job in a datacenter and points at the one part slowing the whole training run, so an event storm becomes one incident. the hot gpu sitting there degrading quietly while everything else looks fine is the whole problem https://t.co/TMrkWPVHFK https://t.co/rPa0aLOklE", "url": "https://x.com/TSC/status/2113427089713955012"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113578334680739840"]}, "author_id": "1977323274511302656", "created_at": "2026-10-23T10:28:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113578343929127254"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 246, "start": 240, "tag": "AIGPU"}, {"end": 258, "start": 247, "tag": "DataCenter"}, {"end": 276, "start": 259, "tag": "AIInfrastructure"}, {"end": 289, "start": 277, "tag": "GPUHardware"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/tcK6EbhSgr", "end": 313, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IDC_HW_Supply/status/2113578343929127254/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113578334680739840", "start": 290, "url": "https://t.co/tcK6EbhSgr"}]}, "id": "2113578343929127254", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "GPU accelerators power AI training &amp; inference.\nLimited stock slows your AI rollout.\n\nReliable data center GPUs:\n✅ A100 / H100 / L40S\n✅ Stable bulk supply\n✅ Ship to EU &amp; NA\nWhich model are you sourcing?\nDM for specs &amp; lead time\n#AIGPU #DataCenter #AIInfrastructure #GPUHardware https://t.co/tcK6EbhSgr", "url": "https://x.com/IDC_HW_Supply/status/2113578343929127254"}, {"author_id": "2107951368082186241", "created_at": "2026-10-22T00:55:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113071805229355423"], "id": "2113071805229355423", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "News observation · Baseline BL-4fffec3e32bafd11\n\nIn its European DSX ecosystem announcement, NVIDIA described cooling and power-management designs and reported tests involving Lambda and Nscale. The source reading record dates the announcement to October 21, 2026, but the", "url": "https://x.com/signalcask/status/2113071805229355423"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113460849461592064"]}, "author_id": "164695180", "created_at": "2026-10-23T03:18:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113470159847604555"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 6, "id": "998897550827642880", "start": 0, "username": "ionet"}], "urls": [{"description": "A gallery full of images created with Stable Diffusion and Kandinsky. Check out the images and their metadata including their prompt, negative prompt, inference steps, guidance scale, and seed. Generate similar images directly from the gallery or submit your own.", "display_url": "BC8.ai", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://BC8.ai", "start": 257, "status": 200, "title": "Gallery | BC8", "unwound_url": "https://BC8.ai", "url": "https://t.co/EK5qXTf1P0"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/cy0T5xo0kM", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/awiblanco/status/2113470159847604555/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113460849461592064", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/cy0T5xo0kM"}]}, "id": "2113470159847604555", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 147, "like_count": 21, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "@ionet through IO Intelligence just crossed 1 trillion tokens processed!!\n\nNo massive budgets, no gigawatt campuses just GPU capacity switched on and put to real use.\n\nThe path wasn’t straight. \n\nSeveral products that were nearly ready for launch including https://t.co/EK5qXTf1P0 https://t.co/cy0T5xo0kM", "url": "https://x.com/awiblanco/status/2113470159847604555"}, {"author_id": "1955999471218614272", "created_at": "2026-10-22T19:01:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113344891954565603"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 12, "start": 7, "tag": "IREN"}, {"end": 20, "start": 15, "tag": "NVDA"}], "urls": [{"description": "Building an AI factory is one thing. Keeping it running at peak eff...", "display_url": "youtube.com/watch?v=AYGSUv…", "end": 204, "expanded_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AYGSUv-EAfY", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113344894919962624/tCzqb5AU?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113344894919962624/tCzqb5AU?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 181, "status": 200, "title": "NVIDIA Minerva: The AI-Native AIOps Platform for Maximizing AI Factory Yield", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AYGSUv-EAfY", "url": "https://t.co/CGduV2TQEq"}]}, "id": "2113344891954565603", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 2500, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Hidden $IREN x $NVDA Webinar featuring Jason Forrester, IREN's VP of Cloud\n\n\"NVIDIA Minerva: The AI-Native AIOps Platform for Maximizing AI Factory Yield\"\n\n(unlisted YouTube video: https://t.co/CGduV2TQEq)\n\nNVIDIA launched Minerva today, an AIOps platform designed to keep AI", "url": "https://x.com/kap_investings/status/2113344891954565603"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113659245933502464", "3_2113659245899997184", "3_2113659245941915648", "3_2113659245954555905"]}, "author_id": "2113640602977841152", "created_at": "2026-10-23T15:50:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113659438582075887"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "66780587", "start": 0, "username": "awscloud"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/1j9UZQQ6AY", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659245933502464", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/1j9UZQQ6AY", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659245899997184", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/1j9UZQQ6AY", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659245941915648", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/1j9UZQQ6AY", "end": 280, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113659245954555905", "start": 257, "url": "https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY"}]}, "id": "2113659438582075887", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@awscloud just made SageMaker training session APIs generally available, and the abstraction is the story: GPU operations are now API calls. forward_backward(), optim_step(), sample(), composed from your own Python. The cluster is not your problem anymore. https://t.co/1j9UZQQ6AY", "url": "https://x.com/getdailycommit/status/2113659438582075887"}, {"author_id": "1919280570372435968", "created_at": "2026-10-23T12:15:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113605105857568929"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 177, "start": 174, "tag": "AI"}], "urls": [{"description": "AWS’s new SageMaker Training Session APIs let developers customize AI models for tool use, workflows, and agent behavior while AWS manages GPUs, distributed training, recovery, and checkpoints.", "display_url": "spaisee.com/article/aws-tu…", "end": 201, "expanded_url": "https://spaisee.com/article/aws-turns-sagemaker-into-a-managed-lab-for-training-ai-agents", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113605114116120576/0YhnCyZh?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113605114116120576/0YhnCyZh?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 178, "status": 200, "title": "AWS Makes SageMaker a Managed Lab for Training AI Agents", "unwound_url": "https://spaisee.com/article/aws-turns-sagemaker-into-a-managed-lab-for-training-ai-agents", "url": "https://t.co/XrlGVN1H6E"}]}, "id": "2113605105857568929", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "The hardest part of training an AI agent may not be the GPU cluster: it’s the reward function. A claims agent rewarded for speed could learn to route cases too aggressively. #AI https://t.co/XrlGVN1H6E", "url": "https://x.com/spaisee_com/status/2113605105857568929"}, {"author_id": "195620273", "created_at": "2026-10-23T18:24:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113698118055383068"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Explore this post and more from the LocalLLaMA community", "display_url": "reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/c…", "end": 239, "expanded_url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1xdlj42/heres_where_the_last_rtx_5090_cards_are_going/", "images": [{"height": 584, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113698118424543232/DDImGQZp?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1120}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113698118424543232/DDImGQZp?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 216, "status": 200, "title": "From the LocalLLaMA community on Reddit: Here's where the last RTX 5090 cards are going: Massive AI conversion factory exposed in China, Founders Edition included", "unwound_url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1xdlj42/heres_where_the_last_rtx_5090_cards_are_going/", "url": "https://t.co/eUdRi4YR7v"}]}, "id": "2113698118055383068", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Where did the last RTX 5090s go? A massive conversion factory in China is stripping consumer cards — Founders Edition included — and rebuilding them for AI workloads. Your GPU shortage is someone's training cluster. https://t.co/eUdRi4YR7v", "url": "https://x.com/DanteMMartin/status/2113698118055383068"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113194275450101761"]}, "author_id": "299599858", "created_at": "2026-10-22T09:03:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113194458787594743"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 115, "id": "998897550827642880", "start": 109, "username": "ionet"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/pG4Wf0ov34", "end": 139, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/fekuuuu/status/2113194458787594743/video/1", "media_key": "13_2113194275450101761", "start": 116, "url": "https://t.co/pG4Wf0ov34"}]}, "id": "2113194458787594743", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 166, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Follow one task through the machine:\nGPU → provider network → your cluster → training &amp; inference\nThat’s @ionet https://t.co/pG4Wf0ov34", "url": "https://x.com/fekuuuu/status/2113194458787594743"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113506024430702592"]}, "author_id": "1028566154758029313", "created_at": "2026-10-23T14:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113639080533557621"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "This session explores how full-stack optimization across compute, networking, and software can unlock higher GPU utilization, faster training, and more predictable performance in AMD-based AI clusters. Attendees will learn practical design principles for building high-performance Ethernet fabrics, reducing bottlenecks, and optimizing the complete AI stack, from GPU communication to cluster-scale architecture. Ideal for enterprise infrastructure leaders planning or expanding AI deployments.", "display_url": "onug.net/events/ai-netw…", "end": 253, "expanded_url": "https://onug.net/events/ai-networking-full-stack-optimization-for-amd-clusters-drivenets-triple-t/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113639127778217984/IEBfyaZl?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113639127778217984/IEBfyaZl?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 230, "status": 200, "title": "AI Networking & Full-stack Optimization for AMD Clusters - DriveNets Triple-T - ONUG", "unwound_url": "https://onug.net/events/ai-networking-full-stack-optimization-for-amd-clusters-drivenets-triple-t/", "url": "https://t.co/mN7W8SvU2x"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Nykx5b9L1c", "end": 305, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2113639080533557621/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113506024430702592", "start": 282, "url": "https://t.co/Nykx5b9L1c"}]}, "id": "2113639080533557621", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 36, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Come by our booth at the ONUG AI Networking Summit and talk to our AI infrastructure experts - Sagie Fanish and Shai Haim\n\nJoin our session!\n\n👉 AI Networking &amp; Full-stack Optimization for AMD Clusters\n\nOctober 29 | 2:30 pm ET\nhttps://t.co/mN7W8SvU2x\nIn this session, DriveNets' https://t.co/Nykx5b9L1c", "url": "https://x.com/drivenets/status/2113639080533557621"}, {"author_id": "2005352736834088961", "created_at": "2026-10-22T01:45:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113084325222810036"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/credosemi/stat…", "end": 269, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/credosemi/status/2112970780879523849", "start": 246, "url": "https://t.co/pKZwCWDkPj"}]}, "id": "2113084325222810036", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112970780879523849", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "\"Wide and slow\" is a smart answer for mid-range AI fabric links. In a big GPU cluster one flapping cable can stall a whole training job, so link stability matters as much as raw speed. Curious how ALCs compare to AECs on power and cost at scale. https://t.co/pKZwCWDkPj", "url": "https://x.com/SuhasDasari/status/2113084325222810036"}, {"author_id": "1057502892310048768", "created_at": "2026-10-22T12:39:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113248885044846822"], "id": "2113248885044846822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "System delivery and training goodput\n\nNVIDIA’s DSX POD could shorten one part of AI data-center deployment. It cannot make a cluster production-ready by itself.\n\nNVIDIA’s reference design shifts rack-to-rack cabling, wiring, piping, rack-level power and liquid-cooling", "url": "https://x.com/ElioJackee/status/2113248885044846822"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113597055658762240"]}, "author_id": "1711723363792805888", "created_at": "2026-10-23T11:43:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113597084066799828"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/D9rD8ojYqq", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/The_Tradesman1/status/2113597084066799828/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113597055658762240", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/D9rD8ojYqq"}]}, "id": "2113597084066799828", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 165, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "💻 Chennai is set to host one of the world's largest AMD GPU clusters, with  Vultr deploying a massive 20MW supercluster featuring AMD Instinct MI355X accelerators. \n\nMarking India's largest AMD deployment and